WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.060
Hey, it's Bluebold!

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.760
Sentences wear disguises.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.360
Today we're unmasking the real subject.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.460
The box of pencils,

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.180
is or are on the desk?

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.180
Your ear hears pencils,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.820
and wants to say are.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.720
That's the trap.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.020
So cross out the phrase in the middle,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.100
just for a moment.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.940
Of pencils, gone.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:23.920
Now what's left?

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.060
The box. The subject is box,

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.920
not pencils. One box.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.540
So, is. The box is on the desk.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.700
A verb agrees in number with its subject,

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.720
not with whatever noun happens to be standing next to it.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.260
Think of a seesaw:

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.740
subject on one side,

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:42.820
verb on the other.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.100
Two boxes, are.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.060
Level. Take one away,

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:46.960
and it tips.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.060
Switch to is,

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:48.960
level again.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.150
Now stand pencils right beside it.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.930
Nothing moves. It only weighs the subject.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.450
Your turn. The list of chores,

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.930
is or are long?

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:00.830
Go.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.450
Is! Cross out of chores.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:09.870
One list, so,

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.570
is. The list is long.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.350
But don't cross out too much.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.170
The box and the bag are on the desk.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.350
Cross out and the bag,

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.490
and you lose a subject.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.550
Two things joined by and:

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:23.770
that's two subjects.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:24.970
So, are.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:28.090
Nearby plurals are decoys.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.450
They distract you from a singular subject.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:31.990
Cross out the phrase,

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.290
then match subject and verb.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.330
Now hit Try this skill,

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.590
and go unmask them!
